---
import Footer from "@/components/Footer.astro";
import Nav from "@/components/Nav.astro";
import Layout from "@/layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="Security | Shellular"
  description="How Shellular keeps your terminals, file systems, and AI agents secure: end-to-end encryption, device approval, and open source."
  keywords={["Shellular security", "end-to-end encrypted", "open source relay", "device approval"]}
>
  <Nav />
  <main class="legal-page">
    <div class="legal-container">
      <header class="legal-header">
        <h1>Security</h1>
        <p class="meta">
          Shellular lets you control your entire dev environment from your phone. Here's how we keep that safe.
        </p>
      </header>

      <div class="legal-body">
        <section class="short-version">
          <h2 data-num="TL;DR">The short version</h2>
          <ul>
            <li>
              Your data is end-to-end encrypted. The encryption key lives only on your device and never travels over the
              network, not even to our relay.
            </li>
            <li>
              New devices can't connect automatically. Every new device must be explicitly approved from the host
              machine before it gets access.
            </li>
            <li>
              You can lock the host to specific accounts. An optional allowlist restricts connections to the exact
              Shellular accounts you name, and turns unauthenticated clients away entirely.
            </li>
            <li>
              The relay, CLI, and app are <a
                href="https://github.com/orgs/shellular-org/repositories"
                target="_blank"
                rel="noopener noreferrer">all open source</a
              >. You can read the code, audit it, or self-host the entire thing.
            </li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 data-num="01">How it works</h2>
          <p>Shellular has three parts:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>
              <strong>Host (CLI)</strong>: runs on your machine or VPS. This is where your terminals, files, and agents actually
              live.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Relay</strong>: a lightweight open source server that forwards encrypted traffic between your host
              and your phone. It cannot read your data; it only passes encrypted bytes through.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Mobile app</strong>: connects to your host via the relay, using the key generated on your host.
            </li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            Because the encryption key is generated and stored only on the host device, the relay (and by extension, us)
            has no way to decrypt your session, even if we wanted to.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 data-num="02">Device approval</h2>
          <p>
            The first time a new device tries to connect to your host, it does not get in automatically. You have to
            explicitly approve it from the host machine.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 data-num="03">Account allowlist</h2>
          <p>
            Device approval is per device. On top of it, you can add a second gate that works per <strong>account</strong>,
            the Shellular account you sign in with in the app.
          </p>
          <p>
            The allowlist is off by default, so any approved device connects as usual. The moment you add the first
            account with <code>shellular users add</code>, it switches on: from then on, only the accounts you've listed
            can connect, and any unauthenticated client is turned away. Remove an account and every one of its devices is
            disconnected at once.
          </p>
          <p>
            It's a clean way to lock a shared or always-on host, like a VPS, to just your own accounts, without having
            to approve each device by hand. See the <a href="/docs#user-allowlist">CLI docs</a> for the full command set.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 data-num="04">Self-hosting</h2>
          <p>
            If you'd rather not rely on our hosted relay at all, you can run your own relay on your own infrastructure.
            The relay is open source. The <a
              href="https://github.com/shellular-org/server"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener noreferrer">server README</a
            > is the best starting point.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 data-num="05">Open source and verifiable</h2>
          <p>
            The CLI, relay, and mobile app source code are all publicly available. The server exposes the running commit
            SHA at <code>api.shellular.dev</code>. The CLI publishes to NPM via GitHub Actions, so you can verify any
            release by cross-referencing the changelog and the Actions run that produced it.
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li>
              <strong>App</strong>: <a
                href="https://github.com/shellular-org/app"
                target="_blank"
                rel="noopener noreferrer">github.com/shellular-org/app</a
              >
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>CLI</strong>: <a
                href="https://github.com/shellular-org/packages"
                target="_blank"
                rel="noopener noreferrer">github.com/shellular-org/packages</a
              >
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Server</strong>: <a
                href="https://github.com/shellular-org/server"
                target="_blank"
                rel="noopener noreferrer">github.com/shellular-org/server</a
              >
            </li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 data-num="06">What we don't have yet</h2>
          <p>
            We're an early-stage startup. We don't have SOC 2 or ISO 27001 certifications yet. We're not going to
            pretend otherwise.
          </p>
          <p>
            What we do have is fully open source, auditable code and an architecture designed so that even our own
            servers never see your unencrypted data.
          </p>
          <p>
            If your team needs something specific for a vendor review that isn't covered here, email us at <a
              href="mailto:team@shellular.dev">team@shellular.dev</a
            > and we'll get back to you directly.
          </p>
        </section>
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Layout>

<style>
  .legal-page {
    position: relative;
    min-height: 80vh;
    padding: 140px clamp(16px, 6vw, 64px) 96px;
    background: var(--cream-100);
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .legal-page::before {
    content: "";
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0 0 auto 0;
    height: 360px;
    background:
      radial-gradient(ellipse 80% 70% at 50% -10%, rgba(255, 240, 210, 0.5) 0%, transparent 60%),
      linear-gradient(180deg, var(--sky-100) 0%, transparent 100%);
    pointer-events: none;
  }

  .legal-container {
    position: relative;
    max-width: 760px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    z-index: 1;
  }

  .legal-header {
    margin-bottom: 56px;
    text-align: center;
  }

  .legal-header h1 {
    font-family: "Plus Jakarta Sans", "Inter", sans-serif;
    font-size: clamp(2.2rem, 5.5vw, 3.4rem);
    font-weight: 800;
    letter-spacing: -0.04em;
    line-height: 1.04;
    color: var(--ink-900);
    margin-bottom: 14px;
  }

  .meta {
    display: block;
    font-size: 15px;
    color: var(--ink-500);
    line-height: 1.7;
    max-width: 560px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .legal-body {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 16px;
  }

  section {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    padding: clamp(24px, 4vw, 36px);
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-sm);
    transition: box-shadow 0.25s ease;
  }

  section:hover {
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-md);
  }

  .short-version {
    background: var(--sky-100);
    border-color: rgba(21, 108, 194, 0.16);
  }

  .short-version h2::before {
    background: rgba(21, 108, 194, 0.12);
    color: var(--accent-blue);
  }

  h2 {
    font-family: "Plus Jakarta Sans", "Inter", sans-serif;
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--ink-900);
    margin-bottom: 16px;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    display: flex;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: 12px;
  }

  h2::before {
    content: attr(data-num);
    font-family: "Fragment Mono", "JetBrains Mono", monospace;
    font-size: 11px;
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    color: var(--brand-gold-deep);
    padding: 3px 8px;
    background: rgba(var(--brand-gold-rgb), 0.14);
    border-radius: 6px;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  p {
    font-size: 15px;
    color: var(--ink-700);
    line-height: 1.75;
    margin-bottom: 12px;
  }

  p:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  ul {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 10px;
    margin-bottom: 12px;
  }

  ul li {
    font-size: 15px;
    color: var(--ink-700);
    line-height: 1.7;
    padding-left: 22px;
    position: relative;
  }

  ul li::before {
    content: "";
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    top: 12px;
    width: 10px;
    height: 1px;
    background: var(--brand-gold-deep);
  }

  strong {
    color: var(--ink-900);
    font-weight: 700;
  }

  code {
    font-family: "Fragment Mono", "JetBrains Mono", monospace;
    font-size: 13px;
    background: rgba(var(--brand-gold-rgb), 0.14);
    border: 1px solid rgba(var(--brand-gold-rgb), 0.28);
    padding: 1px 7px;
    border-radius: 5px;
    color: var(--brand-gold-ink);
  }

  a {
    color: var(--accent-blue);
    text-decoration: none;
    border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(21, 108, 194, 0.3);
    transition:
      color 0.18s ease,
      border-color 0.18s ease;
  }

  a:hover {
    color: var(--accent-orange);
    border-bottom-color: var(--accent-orange);
  }

  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    h2 {
      flex-wrap: wrap;
    }
  }
</style>
